          ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
          ":question/problem": "An ellipse has center $(-6,-3)$, horizontal radius $4$ and vertical radius $3$.\n\nWhich set of parametric equations generates this ellipse for $0\\leq\\theta<2\\pi$?",
          ":question/worked-solution": "An ellipse with center $(h,k)$, horizontal radius $a$ and vertical radius $b$ has the standard parametrization\n\n$$\nx=h+a\\cos\\theta,\\qquad y=k+b\\sin\\theta,\\qquad 0\\leq\\theta<2\\pi.\n$$\n\nHere $h=-6$, $k=-3$, $a=4$ and $b=3$. Substituting gives\n\n$$\nx=4\\cos\\theta-6,\\,y=3\\sin\\theta-3,\\qquad 0\\leq\\theta<2\\pi.\n$$",
